{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>Let there be light, and there was light.</b> Why does it not write ויהי כן, as with the others? Because with the others, כן is written to shorten its words — for had it spelled out every order of the creation it would have had to run long; but here there is no more length in the words ויהי אור than in the words ויהי כן."], :book :genesis, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T23:15:35.189836099Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}